{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And My anger shall be kindled.</b> The attribute of judgment that smote Egypt in order to bring you out — for you were strangers. And He said this corresponding to the stranger (ger) whom He mentioned. And He said, <b>and your wives shall be widows,</b> corresponding to 'every widow'; <b>and your children orphans,</b> corresponding to 'the orphan' — everything measure for measure. And all the time that you are careful with them and have compassion upon them, the attribute of judgment will turn into mercy, for the attribute of goodness is greater than the attribute of punishment; and through this you will lengthen your days, you and your children, and charity will be yours before HaShem, may He be exalted, for the fruit of charity is length of days, as is said (Proverbs 10): ״וצדקה תציל ממות״, and it is written (ibid. 12): ״בארח צדקה חיים ודרך נתיבה אל מות״, and great is charity more than the sacrifices, as is said (ibid. 21): ״עשה צדקה ומשפט נבחר לה' מזבח״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "הש\"י resolved as HaShem, may He be exalted, per the reverent abbreviation pattern. Proverbs citations given as (משלי י), (שם יב), (שם כא) rendered with chapter numbers and 'ibid.' where שם is used; verse content matches Proverbs 10:2, 12:28, and 21:3 respectively."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:05.175595132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}